RF.put("questb:b9",{"8169":{"id":8169,"t":"The Battle for Arathi Basin!","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assault the Arathi Basin mine, lumber mill, blacksmith and stable, and then return to Deathmaster Dwire in Hammerfall.\nMine Assaulted\nLumber Mill Assaulted\nBlacksmith Assaulted\nStable Assaulted","desc":"As you no doubt have heard, the League of Arathor is sending large numbers of troops into Arathi Basin. Eager for food and supplies, these Alliance fools are intent to take and control the rich resources there. We must show them that Arathi will never again be a home for humans!\nGo to Arathi Basin and assault the mine, the lumber mill, the blacksmith and the stables. Pull down the enemies' banners, declaring those territories for the Horde.\nGo, ‹name›. Report back to me when this task is complete.","rew":"Money: 1 30 1 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+200 reputation with The Defilers","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.3,"y":29.7,"n":"Deathmaster Dwire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8729":{"id":8729,"t":"The Wrath of Neptulon","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Arcanite Buoy at the Swirling Maelstrom at the Bay of Storms in Azshara.\nBlue Scepter Shard Maws 49 %\nProvided: Arcanite Buoy","desc":"Did I mention the bad news yet? Its name is Maws: 100 feet of death and destruction. I guess I may have forgotten that little tidbit.\nAccording to my superior psycho-psionic clairvoyance, you'll find that the best spot to cast this buoy is off the coast of Azshara, in the Bay of Storms.\nLook for a swirling maelstrom, most likely cluttered with wreckage.\nBy the by, I hope you have friends.\nNow if you somehow miraculously succeed, take the scepter shard to Anachronos.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBand of Icy Depths Darkwater Robes\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Time is running out, champion.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. I will be able to reform the Scepter of the Shifting Sands soon.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"4729":{"id":4729,"t":"Kibler's Exotic Pets","lv":59,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and find Bloodaxe Worg Pups. Use the cage to carry the ferocious little beasts. Bring back a Caged Worg Pup to Kibler.\nCaged Worg Pup\nProvided: Empty Worg Pup Cage","desc":"You're probably wondering what I'm doing out here. Look at the cages! Ain't it obvious?\nI'm an animal lover, first and foremost, but a salesman by trade. I track down exotic animals for the rich and famous and domesticate the beasts so they behave as proper pets.\nNow you're probably wondering, \"What can I do for you, Kibler.\" The answer is simple: Take this here beast cage and find me some worg pups. For that, I'll domesticate a worg for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nWorg Carrier\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400","back":"<Kibler is busy arguing with Toucan Stan.>","done":"You got 'em at the perfect time, ‹name›. Any later and they'd be untrainable! Gimmie a minute and I'll have the little fella ready for you to take home.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.9,"y":21.9,"n":"Kibler","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"6569":{"id":6569,"t":"Oculus Illusions","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and collect 20 Black Dragonspawn Eyes. Return to Myranda the Hag when the task is complete.\n20 Black Dragonspawn Eye Rookery Hatcher 80 % , Rage Talon Fire Tongue 80 % , Rage Talon Captain 80 % , Rage Talon Dragon Guard 80 % and 4 more","desc":"So the ‹race› wishes to become one of the Black Flight, eh?\nThe creation of the illusion you require is trivial, but the components required for the divination are quite difficult to obtain. The Warchief has entrusted you with this mission, so Myranda must assume you as capable.\nTravel to the upper citadel of Blackrock Spire and slay enough of the black dragonspawn to fill up one of your packs with their eyes.\nReturn to Myranda when you have gathered enough of the reagent.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"The eyes of that which we wish to mimic are the most important ingredient of any illusion, ‹name›.\n<Myranda points to a bag almost overflowing with eyeballs labeled 'Scarlet Crusade.'>\n<Myranda laughs.>","done":"Let Myranda have a look, ‹race›.\nOh yes, these will do nicely.\nWith these reagents, Myranda will create for you a medallion that will grant an illusion capable of fooling the black dragonflight's gatekeeper.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":50.8,"y":77.8,"n":"Myranda the Hag","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"97929":{"id":97929,"t":"Camping 101 enchanting","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Mot Dawnstrider in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your enchanting skill to 20","desc":"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":44.8,"y":38.8,"n":"Mot Dawnstrider","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"92489":{"id":92489,"t":"Power overwhelming","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay the Mana Elemental in the City of Dalaran for High Sorcerer Andromath in Stormwind City.\nArcanic Enigma slain","desc":"The Kirin Tor have long been allies of the Alliance. With the destruction of their city at the hands of the arch demon Archimonde, the once proud city of mages has now become reclusive and distrusting of outsiders.\nIn recent years they have begun reconstruction efforts to bring the city of Dalaran back to its former glory. However, reports show they are struggling to contain an outbreak of wayward arcane energies.\nWe must help them disperse these attacks lest we lose one of our most powerful allies.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nViolet Sash Runebound Gloves\nMoney: 1 1 gold, 0 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,400","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.6,"y":81.6,"n":"High Sorcerer Andromath","s":1}],"cats":["city-of-dalaran"]},"94249":{"id":94249,"t":"Craftsmans writ azure silk hood","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Azure Silk Hood\nAzure Silk Hood","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Azure Silk Hood, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"AHHHH! Oh, it just a ‹race›.\nHi ‹race›!","done":"It da hood me order-er-ed!\nMe forgot why wanted in first place, but me take anyway.\nHere, take shiny coin. It fell out of slime monster. Lots and lots of them!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":78.4,"y":68.9,"n":"Cowardly Peon","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94329":{"id":94329,"t":"Craftsmans writ imperial plate chest","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Imperial Plate Chest\nImperial Plate Chest","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Imperial Plate Chest, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Imperial Plate Chest Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94329","cats":["crafting"]},"7929":{"id":7929,"t":"Darkmoon Elementals Deck","lv":55,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Elementals Deck to the Darkmoon Faire when it comes to town.\nElementals Deck","desc":"Now that you have gathered all of the Elemental cards together into a deck, a ninth card mysteriously appears with the same backing as the first eight. On this card is inscribed, \"Return these cards to the Darkmoon Faire and be rewarded.\" You have heard that this faire alternately stops at Mulgore and Goldshire every few months, so you will have to wait until they are here next.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Card: Maelstrom\nExperience: 550\n+150 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"I see that you have managed to complete a deck of elementals! Congratulations!","done":"So you have put together a deck of Elementals. Your gesture of returning it to us will create a tie between you and the Darkmoon that will not soon be forgotten. Allow me to present you with one of the greater darkmoon cards as a small token of our appreciation.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.4,"y":45,"n":"Professor Thaddeus Paleo","e":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.3,"y":70.1,"n":"Professor Thaddeus Paleo","e":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"729":{"id":729,"t":"The Absent Minded Prospector","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel south and check on Prospector Remtravel.","desc":"What an honor it was when Master Greywhisker assigned me to work under the guidance of the great Prospector Remtravel. At the academy in Ironforge everyone knew of Remtravel's great discoveries.\nBut the prospector is rather... um... oblivious ...to his surroundings.\nWe had uncovered evidence of a great society. Horrible golems sprang forth from the ground and overran the site. Remtravel never seemed to notice. I ran back to Auberdine for help.\nPlease travel south and see if the prospector is okay!","rew":"Experience: 1,150\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Hollee. is that you? I need some help chiseling this stone. Hand me my stone brush, I think I see something.\nHey, you're not Hollee! Don't suppose you've seen my stone brush?\nNever mind that now! I promised the League I'd send the mysterious fossil I found. Where did Hollee go?\nSo much work to be done! Now where is that mysterious fossil... and my brush... and Hollee...\nAnd who are you... 'tis no matter, so long as you're here to help.\nLet me know when you're ready to start looking.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":41.8,"n":"Archaeologist Hollee","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":35.7,"y":83.7,"n":"Prospector Remtravel","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98889":{"id":98889,"t":"Conflict at darkspear islands","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor","desc":"The Theramore Expeditionary Force are tenacious and continue to send reinforcements to bolster their position on the Darkspear Islands.\nGo, show them the might of the Horde! Bring me the evidence of your victory in this key battleground and you will be well rewarded.","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Raiders\nLevel 49 , requires level 40 Difficulty 40 45 47 52 60 Side Both factions Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 98889","cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"1369":{"id":1369,"t":"Broken Tears","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\n3 Broken Tears Tear of Theradras\nReach 3000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur","desc":"The Gelkis think our centaur mother, Theradras, protects us. They are stupid. No one protects the centaur. The Magram do not need protection! We are the strongest!\nShow the Gelkis they are stupid. Go to the cave in their village. They hoard crystals in that cave, the tears of Theradras. Destroy the tears and bring me the broken pieces!","rew":"Experience: 2,650","back":"If you are not our enemy, then you will do what I ask!","done":"You got the tears! Now the Gelkis will know that Theradras will not help them. She will not cry when we crush them! The Magram will rule!\nYou are smart to help us, ‹name›. We are the strongest.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":75,"y":68.2,"n":"Warug","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5929":{"id":5929,"t":"Great Bear Spirit","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out the Great Bear Spirit in northwestern Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the bear. When finished, return to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven, Moonglade.","desc":"In the northwest part of Moonglade resides the home of a wise and noble being we call the Great Bear Spirit. For all druids, it has served as a tutor and mentor into the first true natural understanding of the bear. All druids at one point seek the spirit's wisdom, and you shall be no exception.\nGo to the Great Bear Spirit now and learn what it will teach. When it is satisfied with you, return to me here in Nighthaven. We will then see if you have truly taken account of the lessons it teaches.","rew":"Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Dendrite makes another invisible gesture in the air above him as you approach. Another aura of power comes over him. and he smiles ever so slightly.\n\"I sense wisdom in you, young one, that was not present when we first met. You gaze upon me with strength and knowing intent, though this intent is yet not focused. You will now learn to focus your strength and adopt the nature of the bear into your work.\"","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"99049":{"id":99049,"t":"Threat from below","lv":11,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find signs of what attacked Heglan Shadeeye.\nOrcish Dagger\nBanner Scrap\nBroken Bone Trident","desc":"<The nearby area is destroyed with obvious signs of a skirmish. Whatever ambushed Heglan didn't make it out unscathed. There's probably signs nearby of what happened.\nOrgnil will probably want to see any evidence left by the attackers.>","back":"Did you find her?","done":"This banner and blade piece belong to the naga! They must have come down the coast from the north.\nWe cannot let them establish a foothold here. The pressure from both directions would be too much for Razor Hill.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":58.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Heglan Shadeeye","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":52.2,"y":43.2,"n":"Orgnil Soulscar","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"809":{"id":809,"t":"Ak'Zeloth","lv":13,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ak'Zeloth in the Barrens.","desc":"Since the last great war when the Burning Legion was defeated, I have searched for sources of demonic corruption in orc society. The collar you brought me confirms my fears.\nIt belongs to the Burning Blade, a cult that rallies around an item of demonic power. It is called the Demon Seed, and it resides in the Barrens atop Dreadmist Peak. It must be destroyed!\nGo to Far Watch Post, on the border of the Barrens to the west, and speak with my assistant, Ak'Zeloth. He will direct you further.","rew":"Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"Neeru wants the Demon Seed destroyed, does he? Strange...\nVery well. If he wishes the seed gone, then I will tell you how to remove it.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Neeru Fireblade","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":20.1,"n":"Ak'Zeloth","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"9129":{"id":9129,"t":"Core of Elements","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"30 Core of Elements Huricanian 95.7 % , Smoldar 91.6 % , The Windreaver 79.8 % , Dust Stormer 79.3 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nInsignia of the Dawn\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Truth be told, I use the cores to create Frostfire armor. It is the armor used by the mages battling in Naxxramas. Without you and others like you, we would most definitely be losing this war.\nWith that said, bring me more cores and I shall grant you more insignias.","done":"You perform a great service for us, ‹name›. Well done!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"99129":{"id":99129,"t":"A man about a murloc","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Remy \"Two Times\" about Jason's murloc problems.","desc":"Remy mentioned murlocs the other day... I'm pretty sure he hates the little buggers as much as I do.\nHe might have some ideas on how to keep them away from my fish in the future. I'd like to ask you to go chat with him and see if there's anything he can think of.","done":"I've been warning the guards about the murlocs. They won't listen.\nI have a few ideas on how to get back at those critters. I'll need your help getting what I need for it though.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":47.4,"y":62.2,"n":"Jason Mathers","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Remy \"Two Times\"","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"2969":{"id":2969,"t":"Freedom for All Creatures","lv":47,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the Bamboo Cage Key, free the Sprite Darters from the pen in the Grimtotem camp. At least 6 Sprite Darters and Kindal Moonweaver must survive.\nYou have 6 minutes before Kindal decides it is time to retreat and you fail the quest.\nProvided: Bamboo Cage Key","desc":"The filthy Grimtotem clan are capturing faerie dragons, ‹name›. Jer'kai and I have no idea what they plan on doing with them, but they're obviously up to no good.\nWe're not powerful enough to fight our way into the camp and free the captured dragons, but perhaps with your help...\nIf you're willing, and you have some strong friends, release the creatures from their cage with this key and make sure they escape with their lives. I'll be by your side the entire time. Jer'kai will remain here.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Thank Elune, ‹name›! You are a great blessing to us and to the darters you saved. Jer'kai and I would never have been able to help the dragons ourselves--your intervention in the Grimtotem's affairs will be remembered.\nSpeak to Jer'kai now... I have to prepare for our retribution. Just because the faerie dragons are free, it doesn't mean they will remain so. Jer'kai and I will now go on the offensive.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":65.9,"y":45.7,"n":"Kindal Moonweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"3129":{"id":3129,"t":"Weapons of Spirit","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i wants you to wait for a moment while he prepares the weapons.","desc":"Imbuing the muisek into the weapons is a difficult process. Now that I have all of the required materials and the muisek of the creatures that you captured, I may begin. Please wait; I will return in a moment.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nForce of the Hippogryph Spirit of the Faerie Dragon Strength of the Treant Will of the Mountain Giant\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"As promised, you have your choice, ‹name›. The muisek of the creatures has been forever sealed into the power of these weapons.\nYou may now wield their energy as your own. Use it well.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"6089":{"id":6089,"t":"Training the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Holt Thunderhorn on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it.\nTravel to Thunder Bluff. There you must speak to one of our most revered hunters, Holt Thunderhorn. If he deems you worthy, he will give you the ability to train your new pet.\nHolt has bested the most powerful and feared beasts of Azeroth, and commands many strong creatures of his own. His ties to the Earthmother are strong, and you can learn much from him. Good luck, ‹name›.","rew":"You will learn: Training Lesson\nExperience: 420","done":"A young ‹class›, I see. Yes, I can bestow you with the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.\nNow, go forth. May the Earthmother guide you on your path. We shall speak again, at a later date.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":59.6,"n":"Yaw Sharpmane","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":57.3,"y":89.8,"n":"Holt Thunderhorn","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"3449":{"id":3449,"t":"Arcane Runes","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,550 experience instead of 2,650, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Using the Drawing Kit, make rubbings of the Rune of Beth'Amara, the Rune of Jin'yael, the Rune of Markri, and the Rune of Sael'hai before heading to the small island off of the southern peninsula of Azshara and signaling Pilot Xiggs Fuselighter to pick them up.\nRubbing: Rune of Beth'Amara Rune of Beth'Amara\nRubbing: Rune of Jin'yael Rune of Jin'yael\nRubbing: Rune of Markri Rune of Markri\nRubbing: Rune of Sael'hai Rune of Sael'hai\nProvided: Drawing Kit","desc":"Magic was once as revered as Elune herself to some elves. Some of their most powerful mages created runes and tablets citing rules of the arcane and insights into their findings. They would leave these for all to ponder in public places.\nI would very much like rubbings of these runes from the Ruins of Eldarath. I have a kit for you to make the rubbings with, but it will be up to you to find them. Be careful though, the Explorer's League isn't the only one interested in Eldarath.","rew":"Experience: 2,550\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Well, well, well, glad to see you made it out here, ‹name›. Did you get the rubbings for Tymor?\nAs dangerous as this place is, there hasn't been too much action along the coast. That might be on account of the naga swimming underwater, but that's not my problem... I patrol the skies.","done":"Good to see you safe and sound, ‹name›. I hope things weren't too tough for you.\nI'll get these to Tymor right away. He'll be thrilled to take a look at these things.\nGo ahead and toss the flare gun... probably won't be any good to you anymore anyway, and I already got a new one.\nDun Morogh Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.1,"y":21.9,"n":"Tymor","s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8649":{"id":8649,"t":"Stormbrow the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.1,"y":62.7,"n":"Elder Stormbrow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9049":{"id":9049,"t":"Redemption Girdle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Redemption Girdle if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Girdle, 8 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 3 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Girdle Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Heigan the Unclean 0 % in Naxxramas , Noth the Plaguebringer 0 % in Naxxramas\n8 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n3 Nexus Crystal","desc":"You will find the remnants of our fallen heroes on the corpses of the Lords of Naxxramas. Bring those desecrated keepsakes to me along with wartorn plate scraps and crafting materials capable of revitalizing the cursed armor and I shall craft a fine piece of armor for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nRedemption Girdle\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Redemption Girdle.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"649":{"id":649,"t":"Ripple Recovery","lv":48,"min":42,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Malton Droffers in Orgrimmar.","desc":"I've got some salvage work for you, and if you're an aficionado of fine ripple like I am, then you'll love this task. Ripple!\nIt's a drink, you dummy.\nAn abandoned Horde outpost has a stash of Hinterlands Honey Ripple from when they were in business. You can't get fine ripple like that anymore! One of Malton's dummy associates knows the shot, so you'll go out there and bring me a case of packaged ripple, and two for my own collection! Talk to Malton, he'll fill you in on the details.","rew":"Experience: 440","done":"Oh yeah, about the ripple dad wants! He wants to sell the ripple to a tavern here in Orgrimmar, but we'll get more money if it is in its original packaging. I know someone who can do that, and he's in the Hinterlands where the ripple is. But he's, um, a high elf.\nWell, he's a good high elf, as he's not a part of the Alliance. Well, he's not so much a good high elf as he is a drunken high elf. He loves, and I mean LOVES the hooch.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":59.6,"y":36.5,"n":"Dran Droffers","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":59.8,"y":36.9,"n":"Malton Droffers","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"91209":{"id":91209,"t":"Continue your training","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Follow the road east out of Deathknell to find the town of Brill. Report to Shari Stilwell to continue your training.\nReport to Shari Stilwell in Brill","desc":"Lordaeron may not be what it used to be, but our home still needs protection from all manner of threats and it's time for you to go out and face the world. Your next stop should be the town of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades. Go and meet with Shari Stilwell there. She can see to your continued training.\nOne last bit of advice before you go--take extra care as a paladin traveling through Forsaken lands. There are many in the Dark Lady's service who distrust us and our proximity to the light.","done":"Welcome aboard, ‹class›. It's always encouraging to see more of our number roaming these lands. There are many here in Brill in need of assistance from adventurers such as yourself. Seek employment and grow stronger in the light. Return to me whenever you need training.\nWhen you've proven yourself to myself and the people of Brill, I will provide guidance for the next leg of your journey.\nGo with the light, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31,"y":66.2,"n":"Aramis Hammerhand","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.2,"y":52.6,"n":"Shari Stilwell","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"89":{"id":89,"t":"The Everstill Bridge","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Iron Pikes and 5 Iron Rivets to Foreman Oslow in Lakeshire.\n5 Iron Pike Ribchaser 65 % , Redridge Drudger 65 % , Redridge Basher 65 % , Redridge Mystic 65 % and 1 more\n5 Iron Rivet Ribchaser 65 % , Redridge Drudger 65 % , Redridge Basher 65 % , Redridge Mystic 65 % and 1 more","desc":"During the last orc invasion we were forced to smelt our iron down to make bullets, swords and armor. We sent word to Stormwind for a new shipment of materials but a band of Redridge gnolls hijacked the caravan and ran off into the hills behind Lakeshire.\nNow we're coming up short on supplies to get this bridge rebuilt. If you can bring me 5 iron pikes and 5 iron rivets, ‹name›, I'll make sure you're rewarded.\nNow let's get to work!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSmith's Trousers Bridgeworker's Gloves Riding Gloves\nExperience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"This bridge isn't going to build itself! Now where are those iron pikes and iron rivets?","done":"Great work, ‹name›. These supplies will help the bridge effort immensely. We'll get this beauty shored up in no time.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":27.1,"y":48.6,"n":"Foreman Oslow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"169":{"id":169,"t":"Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg","lv":26,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg.","obj":"Kill Gath'Ilzogg and bring his head to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire for the reward.\nHead of Gath'Ilzogg Gath'Ilzogg","desc":"Wanted! Gath'Ilzogg, Leader of the Blackrock attacks on Stonewatch Keep and raids against the township of Lakeshire.\nGath'Ilzogg is extremely dangerous. He is reportedly holed up in the recently conquered keep plotting the Blackrock clan's further crimes against humanity. The orc infestation must be quelled at all costs. A gracious reward will be given to whatever brave soul can deliver the head of Gath'Ilzogg to Magistrate Solomon.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What do you have there, ‹race›?","done":"Fantastic work, ‹name›! Gath'Ilzogg led those brutes into battle, killing many innocent humans. Vindication is ours. This is the first step in reclaiming the keep for the kingdom of Stormwind!","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.5,"y":46.2,"n":"Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"249":{"id":249,"t":"Morganth","lv":27,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Demonhide Bracers, Shadow Gauntlets.","obj":"Defeat Morganth.\nBring his Pendant of Shadow to Theocritus at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest.\nPendant of Shadow Morganth","desc":"After much observation, I have discovered Morganth's plans.\nHe searches for the Scythe of Elune...and he may have found it! If he has, then the Redridge Mountains, and the kingdom of Stormwind, will soon feel his dark might.\nI am not prepared to pit myself against Morganth, but I fear he must be dealt with now. So you must enter the Tower of Ilgalar and face Morganth.\nDefeat him, and bring me his Pendant of Shadow. Do this, and the kingdom will owe you much.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRose Mantle Demonhide Bracers Shadow Gauntlets\nNew in Forever: Demonhide Bracers, Shadow Gauntlets.\nExperience: 2,750\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hurry, ‹name›, before my fears of Morganth spreading his power are made real!","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. In defeating the warlock Morganth, Stormwind is saved from a grave peril.\nI offer you this reward most humbly. And I would bid you peace, if these were peaceful times.\nBut instead, I will bid you luck with your trials, and victory in the conflicts ahead.\nRedridge Mountains Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":79.4,"y":46.8,"n":"Old Lion Statue","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":65.2,"y":69.7,"n":"Theocritus","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8249":{"id":8249,"t":"Junkboxes Needed","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Heavy Junkbox Irondeep Trogg 22.2 % in Alterac Valley , Irondeep Skullthumper 11.1 % , Theramore Guard 8.3 % , Taskmaster Snivvle 0.1 % in Alterac Valley","rew":"You will receive:\n200 Dusksteel Throwing Knife\n+50 reputation with Ravenholdt\n-250 reputation with Syndicate","back":"My rogues need to hone their lockpicking skills, and I need locks of adequate difficulty -- the stuff Zan makes us is unfit for all but the lowliest neophytes.\nTell ya what, if you bring me 5 Heavy Junkboxes, I'll provide you with some of the finest throwing knives known to roguekind.\nYou can unlock the boxes and rifle through them, but you'll have to leave at least a few coins in them... even a rogue in training needs motivation.","done":"May these knives find a place in someone's heart.\nLiterally.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":84.4,"y":80.3,"n":"Fahrad","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"97289":{"id":97289,"t":"Unending torment","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Head of the Baron to the body of Othmar in the Undercity.\nProvided: Head of the Baron","desc":"We craft abomination heads all the time, but this one is special. It belonged to a Grand Marshal of the alliance once. A particularly unpleasant one. The Dark Lady had the pleasure of dispatching of this one herself.\nOoh the secrets it could tell if it could talk. And it can! If we reattach it to an appropriate host.\nGo ahead and place it next to the available body in the next room. But don't attach it. Not yet.","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,650","back":"<The abomination remains lifeless without a head to control it.>","done":"<The body twitches to life, panicking as it relives its final moments.>\nYou...","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.4,"y":69.4,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":46,"y":62.2,"n":"Unfinished Abomination","e":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron"]},"1049":{"id":1049,"t":"Compendium of the Fallen","lv":38,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Compendium of the Fallen from the Monastery in Tirisfal Glades and return to Sage Truthseeker in Thunder Bluff.\nCompendium of the Fallen Compendium of the Fallen in Scarlet Monastery , Rituals of Power 1 % in Scarlet Monastery","desc":"The Earthen Ring had pure intentions towards our plagued brethren. But who is to know the motivations of those whispering in the ears of the Elder Council?\nThe Forsaken whom we have allied with have a history wrought with deceit. Too hasty was our pact. Perhaps Cairne would have been wise to heed the warnings from Orgrimmar.\nDeep within the Scarlet Monastery lies the Compendium of the Fallen, guarded by crazed human zealots. Their method is forged from insanity but their research might prove useful.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nVile Protector Forcestone Buckler Omega Orb\nExperience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Cairne is a brave and noble leader and I would trust him with my own life. But it is others that I do not trust in this political climate.\nOnce I have a chance to gather all the knowledge available I can provide sound council to the Chieftain.\nHave you had a chance to travel to Tirisfal Glades? To the Scarlet Monastery? The Compendium of the Fallen is just one piece in this complicated puzzle...","done":"The Compendium of the Fallen! I was beginning to wonder if the very book existed!\nYou have served the Tauren of Thunder Bluff well, ‹name›. Your dedication shall not be forgotten.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":34.4,"y":46.9,"n":"Sage Truthseeker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scarlet-monastery"]},"5529":{"id":5529,"t":"Plagued Hatchlings","lv":58,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 20 Plagued Hatchlings, then return to Betina Bigglezink at the Light's Hope Chapel.\nPlagued Hatchling slain : 0/ 20 in Scholomance","desc":"The Argent Dawn recently learned that the Scourge are creating their own plagued dragonflight! We must stop them -- if the Scourge gain a force of dragons they'll sweep across Azeroth unchecked!\nTheir necromancers are breeding plagued dragons at the Scholomance, in the middle of Darrowmere Lake.\nGo to the Scholomance and kill as many hatchlings as you can... before they get any bigger!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Get to the Scholomance, ‹name›. Take out those plagued hatchlings before they grow!","done":"Well done, ‹name›! It'll be a long time before they can grow another clutch of dragons.\n...At least, I hope it will!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":49.9,"n":"Betina Bigglezink","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"8969":{"id":8969,"t":"The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth the spirit of Kormok and slay him. Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain with the Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet and the Brazier of Beckoning.\nLeft Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet Mor Grayhoof , Isalien , Jarien , Sothos and 1 more\nBrazier of Beckoning\nKormok slain\nProvided: Brazier of Beckoning","desc":"Now we have what we need, so it's time to discuss who it is that you'll be summoning.\nKormok was ok for an ogre, right up until he turned to necromancy. After that, things got creepy for just about everyone in the outfit. It was no surprise then when he took his piece of the amulet and returned to his new home, Scholomance.\nBut even there, or perhaps especially there, he was not safe from the spectral assassins. They slew him right in front of his master, Ras Frostwhisper.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"I commend you, ‹name›, if you have returned with the left piece of the amulet. If not, however, please take care of that as there is no time to waste, I assure you!","done":"Good work, ‹name›! Kormok wasn't all that bad for an ogre, at least not while he was still alive, so I hope he gets the rest that he deserves. But, there is more work ahead of us.\nUnfortunately, I do not know the location of the one who died with the right piece of the amulet in their possession. But do not fear; in life I was a dabbler in the art of divination, so I have another task for you, which is going to enable us to ferret out the final piece.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"8409":{"id":8409,"t":"Ruined Kegs","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Darkcaller Yanka at the Wickerman Festival in Tirisfal Glade.","desc":"The rotten eggs have been successfully placed inside the keg. Future batches of ale from the Southshore Inn are sure to be ruined!\nYou should now report back to Darkcaller Yanka at the Wickerman Festival in Tirisfal Glade and report your success.","rew":"You will receive:\n15 Hallow's End Pumpkin Treat\nExperience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Horde","done":"Ah, success! You've shown true Hallow's End spirit - FORSAKEN spirit, I should say!\n<Darkcaller Yanka laughs and rubs her hands together.>\nI revel in the fact that Southshore must now feast on bad ale or go without! As for you, take these treats. I believe you will find good use for them!\nHillsbrad Foothills Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.4,"y":59,"n":"Keg","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":55.6,"y":69.9,"n":"Darkcaller Yanka","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"1529":{"id":1529,"t":"Call of Water","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.","desc":"Long has it been since you were last tested, ‹name›. You have shown patience thus far in your studies, but the time has come for you to learn more. The time has come for you to learn about the purity of water.\nSeek out Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. She is along the eastern coast, south of the Southfury River and Ratchet. You will find her there at her fishing hut. Good luck to you, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 775","done":"The wind approaches you quickly from the horizon; the earth is steady beneath your feet; and your spirit is already warmed by fire--I would say it is time for you to learn about the purity of water.\nYour path has led you this far, and your spirit will give you the strength to carry on even further. But the first step is yours to take.\nThunder Bluff The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":25.2,"y":20.5,"n":"Xanis Flameweaver","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"93129":{"id":93129,"t":"Threat of starvation","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 6 Stolen Supplies back to Hagiak at the Magram Front.\n6 Stolen Supplies\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"Since you seem overly eager to help our clan, I am sure you would be willing to fetch some supplies while you are over in the Outcast Hideaway.\nFelling our foes should be enough motivation for a Magram, but I see no reason why we could not profit from the endeavor, too.\nWhen we have the exiles dealt with, we can secure this place for the Magram and raise an army to bring the other clans to their knees!\nLevel 43 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 39 41 46 54 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93129","cats":["shendralas"]},"8809":{"id":8809,"t":"Extraordinary Materials","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Enchanted Thorium Bars and 2 Enchanted Leather to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing IX in order to complete this quest.\n2 Enchanted Thorium Bar\n2 Enchanted Leather sold by Lhara\nLogistics Task Briefing IX\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing IX","desc":"Vargus, Cenarion Hold's blacksmith, has requested enchanted materials to be used in the crafting of powerful weapons for our forces. Obtain these and bring them directly to Vargus so that Cenarion Hold's troops may continue to be well equipped.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Vargus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"1449":{"id":1449,"t":"To The Hinterlands","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with High Thane Falstad Wildhammer at Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands.","desc":"As I mentioned earlier, I attempted to scout the temple on my own from the air. Well, I wasn't exactly alone.\nI traveled to the renowned gryphon aviary at Aerie Peak in The Hinterlands. There I enlisted the aid of one of their finest pilots. The pilot fell off his mount, down into the swamp...\nIn my old age the poor fellow's name eludes me. The master of the aviary would remember, no doubt.\nJourney there and seek out Falstad Wildhammer.\nWe need to find out what happened to that pilot.","rew":"Experience: 1,800","done":"What do you want, laddy/missy? Can't you see I've got problems to take care of here? Who has time to stand around yapping with some ‹race› chatterbox?\nThere are trolls coming out of the woodwork! Make it snappy.\nStormwind City The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":69.5,"y":40.4,"n":"Brohann Caskbelly","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":11.8,"y":46.8,"n":"Falstad Wildhammer","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"569":{"id":569,"t":"The Defense of Grom'gol","lv":37,"min":33,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Aggro'gosh of the Grom'gol base camp wants you to kill 10 Ogre Brutes and 5 Ogre Witch Doctors.\nMosh'Ogg Brute slain : 0/ 10\nMosh'Ogg Witch Doctor slain : 0/ 5","desc":"When we first arrived in this jungle we did not intend to wage war on the local tribes. Our mission to supply Stonard is of the highest priority. But complications have arisen. A local band of ogres has occupied the Mizjah Ruins to the southeast of Grom'gol. Despite warnings, they continue to ambush our supply caravans.\nI am putting you in charge of dealing with these uncooperative ogres.\nTravel to the ruins and attempt to drive them from the area. At the very least it will send a firm message.","rew":"You will receive:\nGrom'gol Buckler\nExperience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you made any progress with the ogres of the Mizjah Ruins yet, ‹class›?","done":"Well done. You have served the Warchief with honor.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":28.9,"n":"Commander Aggro'gosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"329":{"id":329,"t":"The Spy Revealed!","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Muddy Note to Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp.\nMuddy Note\nProvided: Muddy Note","desc":"Among the valuables of the strongbox is a muddy, scribbled note. Although barely legible, it looks to be an itinerary for Private Thorsen. It details his patrol routes, who he speaks with and how he spends his time with the rebels. It's signed with only one letter: -M.\nBut whoever wrote this note must have stayed very close to Thorsen. Whoever wrote this note is the traitor within the rebel camp.","rew":"Experience: 1,400\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you discover who knew Thorsen's secret? Is there a traitor among us?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. This note is the clue we need to root out the traitor!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":49.6,"y":7.6,"n":"Bookie Herod's Strongbox","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3,"n":"Lieutenant Doren","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"489":{"id":489,"t":"Seek Redemption!","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 3 Fel Cones and give them to Zenn Foulhoof outside of Dolanaar.\n3 Fel Cone Fel Cone","desc":"The Council of the Forest has news that you aided Zenn Foulhoof. The satyr is an enemy of the forest. As a ‹race›, you should know better than to defile the forest by killing Nature's creatures.\nYou must redeem yourself in the eyes of the Council if you wish to remain a friend of Teldrassil.\nTeach Foulhoof a lesson and you shall be redeemed. Fel Cones are corrupted seeds that fall from the trees. They billow with green smoke.\nGive some to Foulhoof. He'll think you have brought him a harmless snack.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+200 reputation with Darnassus","back":"What do you have for me, ‹name›? A lovely snack I presume?","done":"Ah, what a sweet ‹race›! I knew you would come in handy!","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.1,"y":57.7,"n":"Syral Bladeleaf","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.5,"y":56.3,"n":"Zenn Foulhoof","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"889":{"id":889,"t":"Spirit of the Wind","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Blood Shard Bristleback Geomancer 49 % , Bristleback Thornweaver 48.8 % , Bristleback Water Seeker 48.7 % , Bristleback Hunter 34 % and 4 more","rew":"You will learn: Spirit of the Wind","back":"Bring Mangletooth 10 blood shards and I will bless you with great speed. You will run with zhevra and the wind will be jealous of you.\nIt will not last long, but it should be enough to help you travel throughout the Barrens.","done":"Good. Go with Agamaggan's spirit as your guide, ‹race›. Return to me if you desire more of Agamaggan's magics.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"3369":{"id":3369,"t":"In Nightmares","lv":25,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 10 instead of 15.","obj":"Bring the Nightmare Shard to Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise.\nNightmare Shard\nProvided: Nightmare Shard","desc":"This shard holds great secrets; it is the pure essence of the Emerald Dream. However, what I see in this shard is not a dream; one would call this sort of a vision a nightmare.\nI do not wish to alarm you, ‹name›, but I think it is best if you deliver this shard into the hands of a wise druid as soon as you can.\nHamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise is who you need to find. Head to Thunder Bluff. I cannot say more.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTalbar Mantle Quagmire Galoshes\nExperience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"May I help you with something?","done":"Falla sent you to me? Well now, let's see that shard that you say she was so hesitant to talk about...\n<Hamuul peers into the shard>\nOh... I didn't... Well.\n‹name›, thank you for delivering this to me. It isn't wise to speak of things such as this, though, I advise you. These are matters that you should not concern yourself with.\nLet's just say that things in the Emerald Dream are not as we thought...\nPerhaps in the future, our paths may cross again.\nThe Barrens Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":48.2,"y":32.8,"n":"Falla Sagewind","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"7849":{"id":7849,"t":"Separation Anxiety","lv":50,"min":46,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 1g 45s instead of 75s.","obj":"Huntsman Markhor at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to recover his twin brother's remains. Find and return Huntsman Malkhor's Skull and Huntsman Malkhor's Bones to Huntsman Markhor.\nMarkhor mentioned that his brother's remains were fed to the oozes and wolves of the Vilebranch. He also mentioned that there is a refuse pit filled with oozes in Jintha'alor as well as a wolf den. Both of these places are near the top of the temple.\nHuntsman Malkhor's Skull Pile of Skulls\nHuntsman Malkhor's Bones Pile of Bones","desc":"Like many in our village, I too have lost a loved one to the wilds. Alas, it was my twin brother Malkhor - taken in the same raid as Torntusk's mate by the Vilebranch.\nSadly, he was not fated to live and was given a swift, brutal execution; his remains fed to the oozes and wolves of the Vilebranch.\nIt is too late to save his life but not too late to save his soul. Recover his remains, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLaquered Wooden Plate Legplates Greenleaf Handwraps\nMoney: 1 45 1 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,900\n+150 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"When I have his remains, I shall take them to Yayo'jin and have them prepared for a proper burial.","done":"My dearest brother, how I will miss you...\nThank you for your assistance, ‹name›. You are truly a hero in my eyes.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":79.2,"y":79.5,"n":"Huntsman Markhor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"409":{"id":409,"t":"Proving Allegiance","lv":12,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain a Candle of Beckoning.\nSummon Lillith Nefara and kill her.\nReturn to Gunther on his island.\nLillith Nefara slain","desc":"You say you are not bound by the will of the Lich King, and the enchantment Bethor placed upon my book corroborates this. But before I believe you I must have proof that you are enemy to the Scourge.\nThere is an old, bloody altar just off the southern coast of this island. it is used by a powerful Scourge agent, Lillith Nefara.\nTake a Candle of Beckoning from this crate here. Light it on the altar and Lillith will awake. Destroy Lillith, and I will believe you are the Lich King's foe.","rew":"Experience: 675\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"I await proof of your allegiance, ‹class›.","done":"You have defeated Lillith Nefara, proving you are an enemy of the Scourge. Incredible.\nI had believed I was the only Undead with free will, but you have shown me there are others who have broken the Lich King's domination.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":68.2,"y":41.9,"n":"Gunther Arcanus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"5049":{"id":5049,"t":"The Jeremiah Blues","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Jeremiah Payson in the Undercity and see if he is in fact Jeremiah Felstone. If he is, then perhaps he'd like the package Janice Felstone made for him.\nJanice's Parcel\nProvided: Janice's Parcel","desc":"From the evidence I am able to muster, the person you seek - and the intended recipient of the parcel - is Jeremiah Payson, the Undercity cockroach vendor.\nI've always been of the opinion that it takes a special gift to sell... cockroaches. No doubt you are on quite the epic sojourn now, mighty ‹class›. I will leave you to your world-shaping endeavors. Allow me, however, to be a part of your magnum opus and reveal that he is located near the bank, suitably groveling under one of the walkways.","rew":"Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Every time someone steps on a cockroach, I cry. Please don't make me cry.","done":"I haven't used that name in years... but yes, at one point in my life - before this glorious unlife - that was my last name.\nYou claim to have known my sister... or rather, have recently spoken to my sister.\nWho's been dead.\nFor four years.\nYou know, if my bones weren't already brittle enough, I'd be tempted to break my foot off on your posterior. You're quite the vulture, aren't you?\nWhat... you have a package for me from my sister?","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":69.8,"y":43.2,"n":"Royal Overseer Bauhaus","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":67.6,"y":44.2,"n":"Jeremiah Payson","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1689":{"id":1689,"t":"The Binding","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 625 experience instead of 650, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Using the Bloodstone Choker, summon and subdue a voidwalker, then return the Bloodstone Choker to Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind.\nSummoned Voidwalker slain\nProvided: Bloodstone Choker","desc":"By retrieving my choker and besting Surena, you've proven that you're at least as capable as she was.\nWith that said, I can tell you're direly in need of training. You can manage the flows of magic, yes, but being a warlock is much more than that.\nI will show you how to command a voidwalker, but before I can, you must call one forth at a summoning circle and subdue it using whatever weapons--physical and magical--you have at your disposal. Use the magic of this choker at the summoning circle below.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Voidwalker\nExperience: 625","back":"I cannot show you how to control a voidwalker until you have overtaken one.","done":"You did better than I expected, ‹name›, but as well as I'd hoped. Now, you can learn to command your subjugated voidwalker, an ally you will find valuable in the trials that are sure to stand before you.\nI have nothing more to teach you at the present, but I am far from done with you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85.2,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4969":{"id":4969,"t":"Knowledge of the Orb of Orahil","lv":35,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.","desc":"Haha! You're doing very well for yourself, young ‹class›.\nGiven time, infernals and dreadlords will bow before you!\nBut until that time comes, you must still rely on weapons forged by the hands of the mortal races.\nYou seem prepared for another such creation, and if you are willing, Menara Voidrender would speak with you! She is near Strahad's tower overlooking the port town of Ratchet. Go there when you are ready.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","done":"Ah, you do seek something more... substantial. I can help you if you truly are prepared.\nIt's a welcome change to see one of our kind seeking more power in forms other than just knowledge.\nSo, do you feel you're ready, ‹name›?\nUndercity The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":86.2,"y":15.9,"n":"Kaal Soulreaper","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4489":{"id":4489,"t":"Summon Felsteed","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.","desc":"You, ‹race›! Come here!\nYou're the one they call ‹name›, yes?\nI thought as much. I will keep this short: you're growing in power, and it has been acknowledged. And now, the time has come that you are rewarded for your efforts.\nGo to the Barrens. There, above Ratchet, you'll find Strahad Farsan--perhaps you remember him? He would have words with you. I wouldn't take long.","done":"So, you've decided to grace my presence again. How kind of you.\nMy acolytes wondered if you'd ever show up. I told them there was no doubt. When power is concerned, you are drawn in like a moth to the flame.\nUndercity The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":86.2,"y":15.9,"n":"Kaal Soulreaper","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"8569":{"id":8569,"t":"Past Efforts in Warsong Gulch","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Warsong Gulch Ribbon of Sacrifice","desc":"Ah, yes! Of course we wouldn't forget about your past accomplishments in Warsong Gulch.","rew":"You will receive:\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Alliance Shareable Yes Quest ID 8569","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"9":{"id":9,"t":"The Killing Fields","lv":15,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Harvester's Pestslayer.","obj":"Farmer Saldean wants you to kill 20 Harvest Watchers.\nHarvest Watcher slain : 0/ 20","desc":"Look at what has happened to this place! These lands were once occupied by good farm folk. But the damned thieves have driven them all off. Not me, though! But it seems some Harvest Watchers have taken over the fields.\nIf you're up for the work, I'd like you to go out and kill twenty of them. Come back when you're done for your pay. If you finish up with the ones in my field, clear them from the neighboring fields as well.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHarvester's Pants Harvester's Robe Harvester's Pestslayer\nNew in Forever: Harvester's Pestslayer.\nExperience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Ah, I see you're back! I hope you've been hard at work clearing those fields of those Harvest Watchers. Have you killed twenty yet?","done":"Good work, friend. You have earned your pay well. Who knows, perhaps Westfall will prosper once again.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56,"y":31.2,"n":"Farmer Saldean","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"4809":{"id":4809,"t":"Chillwind Horns","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Uncracked Chillwind Horns to Felnok Steelspring.\n8 Uncracked Chillwind Horn Fledgling Chillwind 20 % , Chillwind Chimaera 20 % , Chillwind Ravager 20 %","desc":"I have most of what Tinkee needs, but I'm missing one important component, and that's chillwind horns. The horns of the chillwind chimaera in Winterspring are a concentrated source of cold, but only pristine, uncracked horns will do! I'll need a supply of those to complete Tinkee's order.\nBring me the uncracked chillwind horns, and I'll prepare a package for Tinkee.","rew":"Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Everlook","back":"Do you have the chillwind horns, ‹name›?","done":"These are good specimens. They're packed with cold! Let me get some gloves on, then pack them along with the other things Tinkee needs...","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.6,"y":38.6,"n":"Felnok Steelspring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"969":{"id":969,"t":"Luck Be With You","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 4 Frostmaul Shards for Witch Doctor Mau'ari in Everlook.\n4 Frostmaul Shards Kashoch the Reaver , Frostmaul Shards , Frostmaul Preserver 20 % , Frostmaul Giant 20 %","desc":"Ah, I can tell just by lookin' at ya -- you be wantin' to make a lucky charm. Mau'ari always knows!\nTo da south. you'll find a canyon, an' giants made a' solid ice. The giants sometimes be carryin' dem, but ya can always gather da shards yerself from da canyon. These shards have a powerful reflective quality.\nBring back 4 frostmaul shards, and my lucky charm will be yours.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Bring back da shards, and I be tellin' you more!","done":"Ahh, yes... I will make da charm for ya now. Just you wait!","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"94489":{"id":94489,"t":"The wounds of betrayal","lv":12,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Enter the Nightfang Den and heal 7 druids and find Jorel Windsinger in Shadowgale Forest.\nInjured Druids healed : 0/ 7\nFind Jorel Windsinger\nNaaleos Leafwhisper slain\nTelenos Leafwhisper slain\nNayeela Snarlfang slain\nNeyasteel Mossmender slain\nBryaes Galechaser slain\nMithraless Sterngale slain\nBaeo Sharpstrike slain","desc":"I have finished the poultices. Quickly, take them to the druids in the cave, north just across the clearing. I know my brethren are in much more dire condition than I. They are likely too injured to heal their own wounds. There are so few of us shen'dorei druids that every life is precious.\nBefore you go, I have a selfish request. My mate, Jorel Windsinger was in dire condition when I left. Please, see to his wounds if he still lives.","back":"‹class›! You have returned. Were you able to reach my brothers and sisters? Did you find Jorel?","done":"<Elegael's face pales as you relay the fate of Jorel and the condition of the rest of the druids.>\nNo... no! This is far worse than I had--\n<Elegael chokes back a sob, and grits her teeth letting out a pained snarl.>\nThey will pay. They will ALL pay. Anyone who allies with the Al'aketh will feel my wrath! This I swear.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.6,"y":39.2,"n":"Elegael Thornpaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"9209":{"id":9209,"t":"The Savage Guard - Arcanum of Rapidity","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Zanza the Restless in Zul'Gurub wants an Arcanum of Rapidity.\nArcanum of Rapidity","desc":"Zanza can create many ancient troll enchantments with proper components! Have you heard of the Savage Guard? No, of course you haven't. Your mind is addled with the inferior elven magic.\nBring me an arcanum of elven creation so that I may destroy the aberration. Do this and the Savage Guard will be yours.","rew":"You will receive:\nSavage Guard\n+200 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Do you have the arcanum?","done":"The worthless magic in these enchantments fuels my anger. My anger gives me strength.\nBring me more and you shall receive another Savage Guard.\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 9209","cats":["zulgurub"]}});